**Project Overview**

This project will create a model railroad house lighting automation system using an Arduino Nano, a 0.96 OLED display, and an external RTC (Real-Time Clock) module. The system will mimic daily living in a house by turning lights on and off at typical times, simulating a TV with a flickering effect, and displaying the time on the OLED screen. The time will be sped up by a user-defined ratio (default 6:1).

**Hardware Requirements**

* Arduino Nano
* 0.96 OLED display (I2C interface)
* External RTC module (DS3231 or similar)
* 4-6 LEDs for lights (depending on the number of rooms you want to simulate)
* Resistors and wires for connecting LEDs and RTC
* Power supply for Arduino and RTC

**Software Requirements**

* Arduino IDE
* Wire library for I2C communication
* DS3231 library for RTC communication (if using DS3231 module)

