This code works by iterating through the input string and maintaining counters for the number of open and close brackets encountered so far. When it encounters a close bracket, it adds the total distance from the beginning of the string to that position to the cost. After processing the entire string, it adds the remaining open brackets multiplied by 2 to the cost, as these will have a distance of 2 from the corresponding close brackets.

The total cost is then printed to the output.

